-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Manic Miner
  Publisher   Bug-Byte, 1983
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Manic Miner (1983)(Bug-Byte Software).tzx
  MD5         e0e83ec300013f0c326407e1d1c14cc2

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Note        Keys: O and P left and right, SPACE jumps, ENTER starts from the
              title. Willy, the guardians, Eugene, the Skylabs, Kong, the
              items and the portal are hardware sprites, so Willy is no longer
              half the colour of whatever cell he stands in. The caverns and
              the panel stay as the game draws them; the game-over boot and
              the swordfish ending keep their clash. The Bug-Byte release,
              from its tape.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite oxygen
   3  No collision
   4  Fall from any height
   5  No vertical guardians
   6  No horizontal guardians

  From an archive .pok, each checked against this release's code: the lives
  DEC, the air-out jump, the dying flag's store, the fall counter and the two
  guardian routines. Its lines for other releases are left out.

